Before proceeding, let's ensure we understand the concept of a tape diagram and its application in representing ratios. A tape diagram is a visual representation of a ratio, where the total length of the diagram is divided into parts that correspond to the ratio. In this case, the total length will be divided into 7 parts (2 parts milk + 5 parts water), with 2 parts representing the milk and 5 parts representing the water. We will use standard mathematical terminology and Manim animation development terms to create the specification.
</reflection>

